[?2004hroot@3e3cda255ec7:/app# cd /app && cat >> README.md <<'EOF'
[?2004l[?2004h> 
[?2004l[?2004h> ### Delta sync guarantees
[?2004l[?2004h> 
[?2004l[?2004h> Pages are applied in sequence order (upserts and tombstones together), with
[?2004l[?2004h> exact decimal-to-cent conversion and a unique SKU index. Existing append-only
[?2004l[?2004h> catalogs are migrated by retaining the highest feed sequence for each SKU
[?2004l[?2004h> (latest row breaks ties). Each page and its cursor commit in one transaction;
[?2004l[?2004h> a failed page rolls back and the next run resumes after the last committed
[?2004l[?2004h> page. Empty sequence windows do not mean the feed is finished. A run at the
[?2004l[?2004h> current cursor still makes one request to check for new changes.
[?2004l[?2004h> 
[?2004l[?2004h> Under the supplier's v2.3 retirement/reissue rules, a tombstone also ends any
[?2004l[?2004h> merchandising overrides active on its deletion date, setting `ends_on` to the
[?2004l[?2004h> previous day. Override audit rows, unrelated overrides, and future promotions
[?2004l[?2004h> are preserved; the catalog's merchandising deletion guard remains in place.
[?2004l[?2004h> If a tombstone omits `deleted_at`, the sync uses today's date. This prevents
[?2004l[?2004h> reissued SKU codes from inheriting an old product's active promo price.
[?2004l[?2004h> Supplier action-required notices are logged, and HTTP 409 notice gates are
[?2004l[?2004h> retried once at the same cursor with `X-Notice-Ack`. Other errors, including an
[?2004l[?2004h> invalid/expired cursor, stop the run without discarding committed progress.
[?2004l[?2004h> EOF
